# The typed array tracks the length of its buffer, and one iteration shrinks the buffer.
# Fault injection, testing=AssumeInvariantArrayStorage: the iterations of a loop are assumed to leave the storage of arrays and of typed arrays, and therefore their lengths, unchanged.
# So whatever an iteration reads of them is hoisted and read once, before the loop. The iterations after the resize keep reading inside the capacity that the buffer retains.
# With testing=CheckBoundsAtRunTime (--aot-harden=ignore-told-ranges) and with testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime (--aot-harden=proof-checks) the same operations are built in the same places.
# The hoisted values are checked against the cell inside the iteration, and the process crashes with a named error.
# RUN(RIGHT): run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# RIGHT: 1021 6
# RIGHT-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(HELD): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckBoundsAtRunTime,CheckProofsAtRunTime
# HELD: 1021 6
# HELD-NEXT: exited with 0
# The fault in a default build: the program prints a different result, and nothing crashes.
